From 3238f4ae21e396fc5b7488695875acc5c25d654c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Saravanakumar A <asaravanakumar2k3@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 23:57:23 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] drivers: ra: r_usb_device: commit bulk IN zero-length packets

process_pipe_xfer()'s IN path for total_bytes == 0 selects the pipe FIFO
and then only re-asserts BVAL when it happens to already be set:

	*d0fifosel = num;
	if ((*d0fifoctr & R_USB_CFIFOCTR_BVAL_Msk) != 0) {
		*d0fifoctr = R_USB_CFIFOCTR_BVAL_Msk;
	}

For a freshly selected, empty pipe buffer BVAL is 0, so the body is
skipped and BVAL is never written. The controller therefore never
commits the empty buffer, no zero-length packet is transmitted, and no
BRDY interrupt is raised, so process_pipe_brdy() never delivers
USBD_EVENT_XFER_COMPLETE for the transfer.

A bulk IN endpoint then stalls forever after its first ZLP. This is
readily hit through CDC-ACM: usbd_cdc_acm_enable() primes a zero-length
IN transfer, so on ek_ra8d1 (USB high-speed) CDC-ACM TX never starts --
bytes written with uart_fifo_fill() accumulate in the class TX ring and
are never forwarded to the host. Reproduces with the unmodified
zephyr samples/subsys/usb/cdc_acm sample.

Commit the ZLP the same way pipe_xfer_in() does for a short final
packet: select the FIFO, wait for it to be ready, then set BVAL
unconditionally.

Verified on ek_ra8d1: with this change the host receives the CDC-ACM
data the device sends on DTR (0 bytes before); host-to-device bulk OUT
was already fine and still works.

Signed-off-by: Saravanakumar A <asaravanakumar2k3@gmail.com>
---
 .../ra/fsp/src/r_usb_device/r_usb_device.c    | 23 +++++++++++++------
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/ra/fsp/src/r_usb_device/r_usb_device.c b/drivers/ra/fsp/src/r_usb_device/r_usb_device.c
index dd4674b..9f8a5e6 100644
--- a/drivers/ra/fsp/src/r_usb_device/r_usb_device.c
+++ b/drivers/ra/fsp/src/r_usb_device/r_usb_device.c
@@ -1280,13 +1280,22 @@ static inline fsp_err_t process_pipe_xfer (usbd_instance_ctrl_t * const p_ctrl,
         }
         else
         {
-            /* ZLP */
-            *d0fifosel = num;
-
-            if ((*d0fifoctr & R_USB_CFIFOCTR_BVAL_Msk) != 0)
-            {
-                *d0fifoctr = R_USB_CFIFOCTR_BVAL_Msk;
-            }
+            /* ZLP: commit an empty buffer so the controller transmits a
+             * zero-length packet. Select the pipe FIFO, wait until it is
+             * ready for CPU access, then set BVAL - exactly as pipe_xfer_in()
+             * does for a short final packet. The previous code only
+             * re-asserted BVAL when it was already set, so for a freshly
+             * selected (empty) buffer the ZLP was never actually sent and the
+             * BRDY / transfer-complete interrupt never arrived: a bulk IN
+             * endpoint stalls forever after its first ZLP. usbd_cdc_acm
+             * enqueues a ZLP on enable, so CDC-ACM TX never starts.
+             */
+            *d0fifosel = num | R_USB_FIFOSEL_MBW_16BIT |
+                         (BYTE_ORDER == BIG_ENDIAN ? R_USB_FIFOSEL_BIGEND : 0);
+
+            pipe_wait_for_ready(p_ctrl, num);
+
+            *d0fifoctr = R_USB_D0FIFOCTR_BVAL_Msk;
 
             *d0fifosel = 0;
 
